{"id":"c590cdbcf95b245ec81b4adf13ccc080373aee90","axis":"silent","repo":"vimeo/psalm","sha":"c590cdbcf95b245ec81b4adf13ccc080373aee90","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"UPGRADING.md","lines":["@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@"," - [BC] `ArrayObject` and `ArrayIterator` have the class contract `@psalm-capabilities read-props|write-this-props`, and a purity template, `TStorage` (default `write-props`), for what their mutators cost besides writing the object itself: their constructor binds it to `pure` when given an array and to `write-props` when given an object, so a pure function may mutate an `ArrayObject` it created from an array. `exchangeArray()` always needs `write-props`. A class extending them must now declare `@psalm-capabilities read-props|write-this-props` (or fewer) itself, otherwise Psalm reports `ImmutableDependency`, and its methods may not do more (no `io`, `write-props`, …). An override calling a parent mutator can declare `@psalm-purity-template TStorage(write-props) <= write-props`, extend `ArrayObject[TStorage]<TKey, TValue>` and use `@psalm-purity-from-template TStorage`."," - With `rememberPropertyAssignmentsAfterCall=\"false\"`, property refinements now survive `new` and static calls of callees that cannot write properties, and static property refinements survive callees that cannot write globals (previously every `new`/static call, and only callees writing properties, forgot them)."," - `@psalm-purity-template` accepts bounds written as a chain, `lower <= Name(default) <= upper`: an upper bound (`P <= write-props`) and, on classes, a lower bound (`write-this-props <= C`, which the methods depending on `C` may use unconditionally) and a default (`C(pure) <= write-props`); `Closure[_](...)` in a parameter's type declares an implicit purity template; `@psalm-capabilities` accepts type aliases (`@psalm-type`, `@psalm-import-type`). An unknown capability name is now reported as `InvalidDocblock` rather than `MissingDocblockType`.","-- PHP 8.6 partial function application is supported. Plugins see `f(2, ?)` as a `Psalm\\Node\\Expr\\PartialApplication` node holding `f(...)` (`$call`) and the arguments as written (`$args`), never as a call with a `?` placeholder. `getCallArgs()` of `FunctionReturnTypeProviderEvent`, `MethodReturnTypeProviderEvent` and `MethodCapabilitiesProviderEvent`, and `getArgs()` of `DynamicFunctionStorageProviderEvent`, return `[]` for `f(...)` and `f(2, ?)`.","+- PHP 8.6 partial function application is supported. Plugins see `f(2, ?)` as a `Psalm\\Node\\Expr\\PartialApplication` node holding `f(...)` (`$call`) and the arguments as written (`$args`), never as a call with a `?` placeholder, so provider events only meet its first-class callable. `getCallArgs()` of `FunctionReturnTypeProviderEvent`, `MethodReturnTypeProviderEvent` and `MethodCapabilitiesProviderEvent`, and `getArgs()` of `DynamicFunctionStorageProviderEvent`, return `[]` for a first-class callable `f(...)`."," "," - Backwards compatibility for the plugin API is now covered by a separate metapackage, [psalm/psalm-plugin-api](https://packagist.org/packages/psalm/psalm-plugin-api).  "," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/Statements/Expression/Assignment/InstancePropertyAssignmentAnalyzer.php","lines":["@@ -408,6 +408,7 @@ public static function trackPropertyImpurity(","             $property_id,","             $property_storage,","             $context,","+            $property_var_pure_compatible,","         );"," ","         // writing the property of an object reached from global state writes global state","@@ -491,15 +492,10 @@ public static function checkReadonlyPropertyWrite(","         string $property_id,","         PropertyStorage $property_storage,","         Context $context,","+        bool $property_var_pure_compatible,","     ): bool {","         $codebase = $statements_analyzer->getCodebase();"," ","-        $stmt_var_type = $statements_analyzer->node_data->getType($stmt->var);","-","-        $property_var_pure_compatible = $stmt_var_type","-            && $stmt_var_type->reference_free","-            && $stmt_var_type->allow_mutations;","-","         $appearing_property_class = $codebase->properties->getAppearingClassForProperty(","             $property_id,","             true,"],"additions":2,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/Statements/Expression/Call/ArgumentsAnalyzer.php","lines":["@@ -1788,21 +1788,39 @@ private static function evaluateArbitraryParam(","         return null;","     }"," ","-    /**","-     * @param bool $is_call false when the reference is only taken (a partial application binds it): nothing is","-     *     written yet, but PHP already refuses a reference to a readonly property","-     */","-    public static function handleByRefReadonlyArg(","+    private static function handleByRefReadonlyArg(","         StatementsAnalyzer $statements_analyzer,","         Context $context,","         PhpParser\\Node\\Expr\\PropertyFetch $stmt,","         string $fq_class_name,","         string $prop_name,","         ?string $lhs_var_id,","-        bool $is_call = true,","     ): void {","         $property_id = $fq_class_name . '::$' . $prop_name;"," ","+        $declaring_class_storage = self::getDeclaringClassStorage($statements_analyzer, $property_id, $prop_name);","+","+        if ($declaring_class_storage !== null) {","+            InstancePropertyAssignmentAnalyzer::trackPropertyImpurity(","+                $statements_analyzer,","+                $stmt,","+                $property_id,","+                $declaring_class_storage->properties[$prop_name],","+                $declaring_class_storage,","+                $context,","+                $lhs_var_id,","+            );","+        }","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * The storage of the class declaring the property, null when it is unknown","+     */","+    public static function getDeclaringClassStorage(","+        StatementsAnalyzer $st